{"entries":[{"id":"lex:A1:doctor","headword":"doctor","goals":["everyday","general"],"senses":[{"id":"lex:A1:doctor","pos":"noun","gloss":"دکتر؛ پزشک","meaning":"کسی که بیماری‌ها را تشخیص می‌دهد و درمان می‌کند. see a doctor / go to the doctor = پیش دکتر رفتن.","grammar":[{"pattern":"see / go to the doctor","note":"I need to see a doctor."},{"pattern":"at the doctor's","note":"در مطب دکتر"},{"pattern":"Dr + surname","note":"عنوان: Dr Karimi"}],"examples":[{"en":"The doctor is in the hospital.","fa":"دکتر در بیمارستان است."},{"en":"You look ill. You should see a doctor.","fa":"مریض به نظر می‌رسی. باید پیش دکتر بروی."}],"collocations":["see a doctor","go to the doctor","at the doctor's","a family doctor"],"mistake":{"wrong":"I went to doctor yesterday.","right":"I went to the doctor yesterday.","why":"قبل از doctor حرف تعریف لازم است: the doctor یا a doctor."},"pronunciation":{"gb":"/ˈdɒktə/","us":"/ˈdɑːktɚ/"},"check":[{"type":"cloze","id":"c1","text":"My son is ill. I'm taking him to the ___.","answer":"doctor","accept":[],"fa":"پسرم مریض است. دارم او را پیش دکتر می‌برم.","why":"take someone to the doctor."},{"type":"choice","id":"q1","prompt":"My sister is a ___. She works in a big hospital.","options":[{"text":"doctor","ok":true,"why":"بعد از a اسم مفرد."},{"text":"doctors","ok":false,"why":"بعد از a اسم جمع نمی‌آید."},{"text":"hospital","ok":false,"why":"hospital محل کار است، نه شغل."}]},{"type":"produce","id":"p1","prompt":"باید پیش دکتر بروی.","frame":"You should see a ___.","answer":"doctor","accept":[],"why":"see a doctor."}]}],"version":"e25faeb8d26d","order":750,"unit":10,"prerequisites":["lex:A1:health","lex:A1:sick"],"released":false},{"id":"lex:A1:feel","headword":"feel","goals":["everyday","work","study","general"],"senses":[{"id":"lex:A1:feel","pos":"verb","gloss":"احساس کردن؛ حال … داشتن","meaning":"حس یا حالی داشتن: feel happy، feel tired. بعدش صفت می‌آید و با myself نمی‌آید. بی‌قاعده: feel / felt / felt. feel like = حوصلهٔ … داشتن.","grammar":[{"pattern":"feel + adjective","note":"feel tired, feel better"},{"pattern":"How do you feel?","note":"حالت چطور است؟"},{"pattern":"feel like + noun / -ing","note":"I feel like a cup of tea."}],"examples":[{"en":"I feel happy today.","fa":"امروز خوشحالم."},{"en":"I felt tired after the long trip.","fa":"بعد از سفر طولانی خسته بودم."}],"collocations":["feel good","feel better","feel tired","feel like"],"mistake":{"wrong":"I feel myself tired.","right":"I feel tired.","why":"feel با myself نمی‌آید (ترجمهٔ «خودم را خسته احساس می‌کنم»)؛ feel + صفت کافی است."},"pronunciation":{"gb":"/fiːl/; felt /felt/","us":"/fiːl/; felt /felt/"},"check":[{"type":"cloze","id":"c1","text":"I didn't sleep well. I ___ tired today.","answer":"feel","accept":[],"fa":"خوب نخوابیدم. امروز خسته‌ام.","why":"feel + صفت."},{"type":"choice","id":"q1","prompt":"A: How are you? B: I ___ much better, thanks.","options":[{"text":"feel","ok":true,"why":"feel + صفت."},{"text":"feel myself","ok":false,"why":"myself لازم نیست."},{"text":"am feeling me","ok":false,"why":"me لازم نیست."}]},{"type":"produce","id":"p1","prompt":"حوصلهٔ بیرون رفتن ندارم.","frame":"I don't ___ like going out.","answer":"feel","accept":[],"why":"feel like + ing = حوصلهٔ … داشتن."}]}],"version":"e9e5a63abc0c","order":751,"unit":10,"prerequisites":["lex:A1:health"],"released":false},{"id":"lex:A1:happy","headword":"happy","goals":["everyday","work","study","general"],"senses":[{"id":"lex:A1:happy","pos":"adjective","gloss":"خوشحال؛ شاد","meaning":"احساس خوشی و رضایت. در تبریک‌ها هم می‌آید: Happy birthday!","grammar":[{"pattern":"be happy + to + verb","note":"I'm happy to help."},{"pattern":"be happy with + something","note":"راضی بودن: I'm happy with my new job."},{"pattern":"Happy + occasion!","note":"Happy birthday! / Happy New Year!"}],"examples":[{"en":"The children look very happy.","fa":"بچه‌ها خیلی شاد به نظر می‌رسند."},{"en":"Happy birthday, Mina!","fa":"مینا، تولدت مبارک!"}],"collocations":["happy birthday","happy with","happy to help"],"mistake":{"wrong":"I'm happy for my new job.","right":"I'm happy with my new job.","why":"برای رضایت از چیزی happy with درست است؛ happy for someone یعنی برای کسی خوشحال بودن."},"pronunciation":{"gb":"/ˈhæpi/","us":"/ˈhæpi/"},"check":[{"type":"cloze","id":"c1","text":"I'm very ___ to meet you.","answer":"happy","accept":["glad","pleased"],"fa":"از دیدنتان خیلی خوشحالم.","why":"خوشحالی."},{"type":"choice","id":"q1","prompt":"Are you ___ your new flat?","options":[{"text":"happy with","ok":true,"why":"رضایت از چیزی."},{"text":"happy for","ok":false,"why":"for برای خوشحالی به خاطر دیگران است."},{"text":"happy of","ok":false,"why":"این حرف اضافه به کار نمی‌رود."}]},{"type":"produce","id":"p1","prompt":"تولدت مبارک!","frame":"___ birthday!","answer":"Happy","accept":[],"why":"تبریک تولد."}]}],"version":"d373a42eb0c2","order":752,"unit":10,"prerequisites":["lex:A1:feel"],"released":false},{"id":"lex:A1:sad","headword":"sad","goals":["everyday","general"],"senses":[{"id":"lex:A1:sad","pos":"adjective","gloss":"ناراحت؛ غمگین","meaning":"حسِ غم و ناراحتی؛ متضادِ happy. برای چیزی که آدم را غمگین می‌کند هم می‌آید: a sad story.","grammar":[{"pattern":"be / feel sad","note":"ناراحت بودن"},{"pattern":"sad about + thing","note":"ناراحت از …"},{"pattern":"sad – sadder – the saddest","note":"مقایسه"}],"examples":[{"en":"I was sad when my friend moved away.","fa":"وقتی دوستم از اینجا رفت ناراحت شدم."},{"en":"It's a very sad story.","fa":"داستانِ خیلی غم‌انگیزی است."}],"collocations":["feel sad","a sad story","a sad face","very sad"],"mistake":{"wrong":"I am very sadly today.","right":"I am very sad today.","why":"بعد از be صفت می‌آید: sad. sadly قید است."},"pronunciation":{"gb":"/sæd/","us":"/sæd/"},"check":[{"type":"cloze","id":"c1","text":"He lost his dog and he's very ___.","answer":"sad","accept":["unhappy","upset"],"fa":"سگش را گم کرده و خیلی ناراحت است.","why":"sad = ناراحت."},{"type":"choice","id":"q1","prompt":"She's happy, but her brother is ___.","options":[{"text":"